sentences.t:
Hic tamen ille urbem Patavi sedesque locavit
Teucrorum, et genti nomen dedit, armaque fixit
Troia;

sentences.l:
Here yet he the city of Patavium and the homes
of the Teucrians founded, and to the people a name gave, and arms hung up
Trojan;

sentences.t:
cernes urbem et promissa Lavini
moenia, sublimemque feres ad sidera caeli
magnanimum Aenean;

sentences.l:
you will see the city and the promised of Lavinium
walls, and aloft you will bear to the stars of heaven
